        "body": "I decided that upgrading my Raspberry PI from bullseye to bookworm was the easiest way\r\nto get python3.11 and I followed this:\r\n\r\nhttps://www.linuxfordevices.com/tutorials/linux/upgrade-raspberry-pi-os\r\n\r\nNote, for others trying the same, my PI had an another source in /etc/apt/sources.list.d/raspi.list which also needed changing\r\n\r\nMy PI now has 3.11.2 and I think it has automatically removed 3.9.  I now get this error:\r\n\r\nActivating virtual environment...OK\r\n2025-01-01 15:16:03,589 - ERROR    - __main__: Failed to load fhempy\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/opt/fhem/FHEM/bindings/python/bin/start_fhempy.py\", line 141, in <module>\r\n    import fhempy.lib.fhem_pythonbinding as fpb\r\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'fhempy'\r\n2025-01-01 15:16:03,700 - INFO     - __main__: Attempting install of fhempy>=0.1.462\r\n2025-01-01 15:16:04,316 - ERROR    - __main__: Unable to install package fhempy>=0.1.462: /opt/fhem/.fhempy/fhempy_venv/bin/python3: No module named pip\r\n2025-01-01 15:16:04,325 - ERROR    - __main__: Failed to install fhempy, exit now...\r\n\r\nI notice in /opt/fhem/.fhempy/fhempy_venv/bin there is a pip3.9 and python3.9.  Do I need to put python3.9 back?  Or revises these for python3.11?  And if the latter what is the easiest method to do that?  I can't seem to get fhem/fhempy to do this.\r\n\r\nthanks\r\n",
