        "active_lock_reason": null,
        "body": "I've defined a tuya_smartlife and that seems to be all working.  It has found my WiFi Smartlight.  I can turn it on and off but the icon does not change.  I can change the work mode to scene (leds go green), and to music (leds go red), and to colour (leds go blue).  Setting to white does nothing.  Setting work mode to colour and then colour data (to a anything) gives this error:\r\n\r\nFailed to execute function Set: Traceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/opt/fhem/.fhempy/fhempy_venv/lib/python3.9/site-packages/fhempy/lib/fhem_pythonbinding.py\", line 385, in handle_function\r\n    ret = await self.execute_function(hash, fhem_reply_done, nmInstance)\r\n  File \"/opt/fhem/.fhempy/fhempy_venv/lib/python3.9/site-packages/fhempy/lib/fhem_pythonbinding.py\", line 484, in execute_function\r\n    ret = await asyncio.wait_for(\r\n  File \"/usr/lib/python3.9/asyncio/tasks.py\", line 481, in wait_for\r\n    return fut.result()\r\n  File \"/opt/fhem/.fhempy/fhempy_venv/lib/python3.9/site-packages/fhempy/lib/generic.py\", line 208, in Set\r\n    return await utils.handle_set(self._conf_set, self, hash, args, argsh)\r\n  File \"/opt/fhem/.fhempy/fhempy_venv/lib/python3.9/site-packages/fhempy/lib/utils.py\", line 340, in handle_set\r\n    return await fct_call(hash, final_params)\r\n  File \"/opt/fhem/.fhempy/fhempy_venv/lib/python3.9/site-packages/fhempy/lib/tuya_smartlife/tuya_smartlife.py\", line 78, in set_colour_data\r\n    await self.device.set_colour_data(hash, params)\r\n  File \"/opt/fhem/.fhempy/fhempy_venv/lib/python3.9/site-packages/fhempy/lib/tuya_smartlife/tuya_smartlife_device.py\", line 201, in set_colour_data\r\n    if self._t_info[\"category\"] == \"dj\":\r\nTypeError: 'CustomerDevice' object is not subscriptable\r\n\r\nSelecting in set music_data or control_data brings up a text box which will accept numbers or text.  I don't what this wants but anything I try just throws an error like this:\r\n\r\nFailed to execute function Set: Traceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/opt/fhem/.fhempy/fhempy_venv/lib/python3.9/site-packages/fhempy/lib/fhem_pythonbinding.py\", line 385, in handle_function\r\n    ret = await self.execute_function(hash, fhem_reply_done, nmInstance)\r\n  File \"/opt/fhem/.fhempy/fhempy_venv/lib/python3.9/site-packages/fhempy/lib/fhem_pythonbinding.py\", line 484, in execute_function\r\n    ret = await asyncio.wait_for(\r\n  File \"/usr/lib/python3.9/asyncio/tasks.py\", line 481, in wait_for\r\n    return fut.result()\r\n  File \"/opt/fhem/.fhempy/fhempy_venv/lib/python3.9/site-packages/fhempy/lib/generic.py\", line 208, in Set\r\n    return await utils.handle_set(self._conf_set, self, hash, args, argsh)\r\n  File \"/opt/fhem/.fhempy/fhempy_venv/lib/python3.9/site-packages/fhempy/lib/utils.py\", line 340, in handle_set\r\n    return await fct_call(hash, final_params)\r\n  File \"/opt/fhem/.fhempy/fhempy_venv/lib/python3.9/site-packages/fhempy/lib/tuya_smartlife/tuya_smartlife.py\", line 69, in set_json\r\n    await self.device.set_json(hash, params)\r\n  File \"/opt/fhem/.fhempy/fhempy_venv/lib/python3.9/site-packages/fhempy/lib/tuya_smartlife/tuya_smartlife_device.py\", line 190, in set_json\r\n    await self.send_commands(\r\n  File \"/opt/fhem/.fhempy/fhempy_venv/lib/python3.9/site-packages/fhempy/lib/tuya_smartlife/tuya_smartlife_device.py\", line 225, in send_commands\r\n    await self.tuyaiot.send_commands(self._t_deviceid, commands)\r\n  File \"/opt/fhem/.fhempy/fhempy_venv/lib/python3.9/site-packages/fhempy/lib/tuya_smartlife/tuya_smartlife_setup.py\", line 280, in send_commands\r\n    await utils.run_blocking(\r\n  File \"/opt/fhem/.fhempy/fhempy_venv/lib/python3.9/site-packages/fhempy/lib/utils.py\", line 72, in run_blocking\r\n    return await asyncio.get_event_loop().run_in_executor(pool, function)\r\n  File \"/usr/lib/python3.9/concurrent/futures/thread.py\", line 52, in run\r\n    result = self.fn(*self.args, **self.kwargs)\r\n  File \"/opt/fhem/.fhempy/fhempy_venv/lib/python3.9/site-packages/tuya_sharing/manager.py\", line 93, in send_commands\r\n    return self.device_repository.send_commands(device_id, commands)\r\n  File \"/opt/fhem/.fhempy/fhempy_venv/lib/python3.9/site-packages/tuya_sharing/device.py\", line 180, in send_commands\r\n    self.api.post(f\"/v1.1/m/thing/{device_id}/commands\", None, {\"commands\": commands})\r\n  File \"/opt/fhem/.fhempy/fhempy_venv/lib/python3.9/site-packages/tuya_sharing/customerapi.py\", line 192, in post\r\n    return self.__request(\"POST\", path, params, body)\r\n  File \"/opt/fhem/.fhempy/fhempy_venv/lib/python3.9/site-packages/tuya_sharing/customerapi.py\", line 121, in __request\r\n    raise Exception(f\"network error:({ret['code']}) {ret['msg']}\")\r\nException: network error:(SYSTEM_ERROR) Server Error\r\n\r\n",
