        "active_lock_reason": null,
        "body": "Control-R does not seem to open the history widget but I see \r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b4603849-14af-4c9c-96a0-f32b198b6590)\r\n\r\n\r\nMy config in `.zshrc` \r\n\r\n```\r\n## Hishtory\r\nwhich hishtory &>/dev/null && \\\r\n  source $HOME/$HISHTORY_PATH/config.zsh && \\\r\n  eval \"$(hishtory completion zsh)\" && \\\r\n  hishtory enable && \\\r\n  hishtory config-set filter-duplicate-commands true\r\n``` \r\n\r\nIt is enabled\r\n\r\n```\r\nhishtory config-get enable-control-r\r\ntrue\r\n```\r\n\r\nand running\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ hishtory status\r\nhiSHtory: v0.0.318\r\nEnabled: true\r\nSecret Key: xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx\r\nCommit Hash: Unknown\r\n```\r\n\r\n",
