        "labels": [],
        "state": "open",
        "locked": false,
        "assignee": null,
        "assignees": [],
        "milestone": null,
        "comments": 0,
        "created_at": "2025-01-01T15:23:13Z",
        "updated_at": "2025-01-01T15:23:13Z",
        "closed_at": null,
        "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
        "active_lock_reason": null,
        "body": "Commit 07dd764 introduced a bug where members inside constructors aren't linted properly.\r\n\r\nThe fragment for reproducing is simply:\r\n```js\r\nnum = 0; /// @is {number}\r\nvar str:string = testString; ///want_warn\r\n```\r\nThat won't give any warning. The `num` seems to be typed in the tooltip for example but is just not there for comparing types.\r\nIn the test project that would be the `v_constructor_implicit_types` which is failing all the tests,\r\n\r\nWhile debugging, it appears that the type of such constructor vars is always `any` for the type checker. The issue fixed if I comment out the `selfOverride = GmlTypeDef.any;` line in the `GmlLinterFuncLiteral.read`. I am not sure of the purpose of that override down the line so that probably breaks something else.",
